13
00:00:31,755 --> 00:00:32,911
You smell that?

14
00:00:33,061 --> 00:00:35,178
I'm telling you, something's
dead in this car.

15
00:00:35,298 --> 00:00:36,112
It goes away in the winter,

16
00:00:36,205 --> 00:00:37,548
but it reactivates
in the summer.

17
00:00:37,645 --> 00:00:40,505
No, no. The grass, Mike.
Fresh-cut grass.

18
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:42,733
If it's fresh-cut,
you know it's not ours.

19
00:00:43,244 --> 00:00:44,535
Doesn't it just
take you back, though?

20
00:00:44,632 --> 00:00:45,829
That's it right there.

21
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:48,048
You know, it's just that thing,

22
00:00:48,149 --> 00:00:50,953
that feeling of summer that
you can't describe,

23
00:00:51,054 --> 00:00:53,181
you know, "this."

24
00:00:54,492 --> 00:00:56,097
We should have
an amazing summer, Mike.

25
00:00:56,204 --> 00:00:57,712
Let's have an amazing summer.

26
00:00:57,809 --> 00:01:00,389
Yes, let's, my darling.
With our travel budget

27
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:01,871
of whatever's
in the couch cushions,

28
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:03,298
the world is our oyster.

29
00:01:03,407 --> 00:01:05,519
Ugh. It's not just
about money, Mike.

30
00:01:05,656 --> 00:01:07,792
I mean, don't you remember
summer as a kid?

31
00:01:08,055 --> 00:01:10,347
Going to drive-in movies,
playing ghost in the graveyard

32
00:01:10,449 --> 00:01:12,100
till your folks
called you inside?

33
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:14,457
- Oh, yeah. That was a real summer.
- Yeah.

34
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:15,465
I could kill a whole day

35
00:01:15,563 --> 00:01:17,352
just smacking a tennis ball
against the house

36
00:01:17,491 --> 00:01:22,329
and lying on my back,
in the yard, doing this...

37
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:26,786
Love that.
Still can't do that.

38
00:01:26,901 --> 00:01:29,670
Ah, it's not hard, Frankie.
It's all in the thumbs.

39
00:01:29,763 --> 00:01:31,207
You gotta use your thumbs.

40
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,871
<i>Meanwhile, our kids were busy</i>

41
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:35,119
<i>using their thumbs</i>
<i>for other things.</i>

42
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:38,940
Look at this.

43
00:01:39,041 --> 00:01:40,167
Unh-unh.

44
00:01:40,274 --> 00:01:41,738
Come on. Turn 'em off.

45
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:44,567
You're not spending your whole
summer staring at screens.

46
00:01:49,531 --> 00:01:51,781
<i>- I'm going in!</i>
- That goes for the TV, too.

47
00:01:54,786 --> 00:01:56,474
<i>Whoa! Careful!</i>

48
00:01:59,354 --> 00:02:00,693
Out.

49
