68
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:43,947
or whatever it is
they're playing.

69
00:02:44,116 --> 00:02:45,929
I'm pretty sure they're not
playing Pac-Man.

70
00:02:46,068 --> 00:02:48,390
Yeah, the point is,
Axl's gonna be a senior.

71
00:02:48,528 --> 00:02:51,072
This might be the last summer
we're all together as a family.

72
00:02:51,173 --> 00:02:53,172
I just don't want them
clicking it away.

73
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:55,077
We have to reactivate them,

74
00:02:55,563 --> 00:02:58,008
kind of like that smelly
dead thing in the car.

75
00:03:00,085 --> 00:03:01,112
Ugh!

76
00:03:01,576 --> 00:03:02,939
This is so pointless.

77
00:03:03,081 --> 00:03:04,263
It's our summer.

78
00:03:04,365 --> 00:03:06,253
I mean, they're the ones forcing
us to go to school all year.

79
00:03:06,337 --> 00:03:07,524
This is our time to unwind

80
00:03:07,629 --> 00:03:10,373
howsoever and with whatsoever
we choose, right?

81
00:03:10,474 --> 00:03:13,989
Totalmundo. That's not a thing
people really say, is it?

82
00:03:14,119 --> 00:03:16,218
- No.
- Well, I might try to start it.

83
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:19,447
I wouldn't. I know dad acted
like this was his idea,

84
00:03:19,551 --> 00:03:21,152
