201
00:07:33,259 --> 00:07:34,903
Okay, guys. Hey, guys.
Hey! Hey! Hey!

202
00:07:35,028 --> 00:07:36,447
Hey! Why don't you all go
to the swing set?

203
00:07:36,563 --> 00:07:38,035
Uh, 'cause I'm not 6.

204
00:07:38,138 --> 00:07:39,328
Not a suggestion.

205
00:07:39,596 --> 00:07:40,585
- Ugh!
- Go.

206
00:07:40,684 --> 00:07:41,784
Come on.

207
00:07:47,042 --> 00:07:49,483
Why do I feel like this was
more fun when we were kids?

208
00:07:49,616 --> 00:07:51,671
Because when we were kids
we didn't have kids?

209
00:07:51,761 --> 00:07:52,765
Ah.

210
00:08:03,009 --> 00:08:04,709
Axl, do I have anything
on my butt?

211
00:08:04,887 --> 00:08:05,760
No, you're good.

212
00:08:08,034 --> 00:08:09,394
God, this is lame.

213
00:08:09,506 --> 00:08:11,756
Every year, they go through
some kind of midlife crisis.

214
00:08:11,869 --> 00:08:13,963
Thank God their lives are
more than halfway over.

215
00:08:14,107 --> 00:08:16,450
By the way, nice job getting us
kicked out of the car, Sue.

216
00:08:16,584 --> 00:08:19,841
It wasn't my fault. I was trying
to get dad to listen to me,

217
00:08:19,954 --> 00:08:23,746
