with your friends.

236
00:09:01,567 --> 00:09:04,595
There is no way
you're they're <i>favorite.</i>

237
00:09:04,728 --> 00:09:06,838
Oh! There <i>is</i> way!

238
00:09:07,099 --> 00:09:08,382
I'm their firstborn.

239
00:09:08,515 --> 00:09:10,112
I was born when they still
had love to give.

240
00:09:10,228 --> 00:09:11,518
Well, actually, I'm the baby,

241
00:09:11,616 --> 00:09:13,194
so I'm pretty sure
I'm the favorite.

242
00:09:13,304 --> 00:09:16,186
You're a loser who misses
a tomato. I win.

243
00:09:16,436 --> 00:09:19,336
Believe what you want,
but in every book, every movie,

244
00:09:19,441 --> 00:09:21,364
the baby is
always the favorite.

245
00:09:21,708 --> 00:09:23,102
Not when he's an accident.

246
00:09:23,266 --> 00:09:25,102
That is not true. Sue!

247
00:09:25,227 --> 00:09:27,371
They called you "Oops"
till you were 3.

248
00:09:27,562 --> 00:09:30,633
Look, there is two of you,
and I am the only girl.

249
00:09:30,743 --> 00:09:32,479
Everyone knows girls are easier.

250
00:09:32,596 --> 00:09:34,525
I am so, so nice.

251
00:09:34,653 --> 00:09:36,740
I think it's pretty clear
who the favorite would be

252
00:09:36,847 --> 00:09:39,142
if they had a favorite,
which they don't.

253
00:09:39,249 --> 00:09:41,331
Sue, think about it.

254
00:09:41,431 --> 00:09:43,772
What do you really contribute
to this family?

255
00:09:44,012 --> 00:09:46,200
I mean, Oops is
freakishly smart,

256
00:09:46,334 --> 00:09:48,604
I got recruiters all wanting
a piece of the ax,

257
00:09:48,715 --> 00:09:52,910
and hmm, what has Sue Sue Heck
really brought to the party?

258
00:09:53,043 --> 00:09:55,337
Nothing but the huge rust stain
on her butt.

259
00:09:55,590 --> 00:09:56,970
Axl!

260
00:09:57,741 --> 00:09:59,523
Look, clearly, you two
didn't fulfill them,

261
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:00,795
and they were forced
to keep going

262
00:10:00,896 --> 00:10:02,892
until they got what
they wanted-- moi.

263
00:10:03,014 --> 00:10:05,252
You don't know anything.
Neither of you.

264
00:10:05,346 --> 00:10:07,295
Parents don't have
favorite kids!

265
00:10:07,402 --> 00:10:09,396
I'm sorry! They just don't!

266
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:11,159
Least favorite says "what."

267
00:10:11,263 --> 00:10:12,182
What?

268
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:14,619
See, it's funny

269
00:10:14,724 --> 00:10:16,481
because he said
"least favorite says 'what,'"

270
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:18,393
and then you repeated "what"
and--

271
00:10:18,497 --> 00:10:20,483
Don't nerd up my joke, Brick.
Just let it lie.

272
00:10:24,315 --> 00:10:27,222
- This is nice, isn't it?
- Mm-hmm.

273
00:10:27,612 --> 00:10:29,121
We should do more things like this.

274
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:30,837
Why don't we do more things
like this?

275
00:10:30,984 --> 00:10:32,144
I don't know.

276
00:10:32,823 --> 00:10:34,074
Let's worry about
why we don't do it more

277
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,350
when we're not doing it now.
Okay?

278
00:10:36,793 --> 00:10:37,862
Good plan.

279
00:10:39,408 --> 00:10:40,923
Okay, I get the seat behind mom.

280
00:10:41,025 --> 00:10:44,048
- Ah! What? I mean, as long as we--
- Whoo, popcorn!

281
00:10:44,165 --> 00:10:46,516
- There you go. Help yourself...
- Gimme some of that.

282
00:10:46,630 --> 00:10:48,309
- For crying out loud.
- No ranch seasoning?

283
00:10:48,472 --> 00:10:50,275
Whatever. I'll just eat this
till my fires come.

284
00:10:52,075 --> 00:10:53,251
Mom, I really need
to ask you something.

285
00:10:53,347 --> 00:10:54,662
- Shh. Movie's starting.
- Mm.

286
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,143
How can you tell?
Is that the sound?

287
00:10:56,272 --> 00:10:58,328
It's so crackly. Oh, my God.
I can barely hear it.

288
00:10:58,452 --> 00:10:59,930
- Turn it up. Up! Up! Up!
- Okay.

289
00:11:00,046 --> 00:11:01,382
I think I missed the beginning.

290
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:02,794
The credits are
my favorite part.

291
00:11:02,922 --> 00:11:04,530
Can someone rewind it?

292
00:11:04,852 --> 00:11:07,834
Fun to witness the death of
civilization up close, isn't it?

293
00:11:08,132 --> 00:11:09,702
Do you guys have favorite kids?

294
00:11:09,991 --> 00:11:12,124
Mm. I like those Donahues.

295
00:11:12,461 --> 00:11:15,093
No, of us.
Mom, I really want to know this.

296
00:11:15,215 --> 00:11:17,629
Do you guys have favorite kids?

297
00:11:17,732 --> 00:11:20,320
Among us kids,
do you guys have favorites?

298
00:11:20,441 --> 00:11:21,899
Honey, don't be ridiculous.

299
00:11:22,054 --> 00:11:24,897
Parents love all their kids
infinitely.

300
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:27,904
If there's infinite love,
then it's not possible to love

301
00:11:28,035 --> 00:11:31,179
one more than the other, because
infinite love is infinite.

302
00:11:33,169 --> 00:11:34,470
Guess I'd say Axl.

303
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:36,053
- Dad!
- Mike!

304
00:11:36,165 --> 00:11:37,462
What?

305
00:11:37,663 --> 00:11:38,564
Well, no, sure,

306
00:11:38,667 --> 00:11:40,566
the infinite stuff
your mom said...

307
00:11:41,443 --> 00:11:43,226
Yeah, but, I mean,
if I had to pick,

308
00:11:44,043 --> 00:11:46,858
it's-- it's-- I just have more
in common with him, I guess.

309
00:11:48,258 --> 00:11:49,358
What?

310
00:11:49,457 --> 00:11:50,772
Why you staring at me?

311
00:11:51,162 --> 00:11:52,185
I...

312
00:11:52,592 --> 00:11:54,957
We have football,
we hang out together,

313
00:11:55,108 --> 00:11:56,546
talking about sports.

314
00:11:56,681 --> 00:11:59,732
It's not personal.
Just human nature.

315
00:12:01,329 --> 00:12:02,333
What?

316
00:12:02,428 --> 00:12:04,174
Told ya.

317
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:19,239
Ohh.

318
00:12:29,554 --> 00:12:31,240
<i>As June turned into late June,</i>

319
00:12:32,151 --> 00:12:33,866
<i>Brick's tomato plant grew...</i>

320
00:12:35,312 --> 00:12:36,988
<i>And grew...</i>

321
00:12:39,502 --> 00:12:42,821
<i>And finally</i>
<i>turned into a tomato.</i>

322
00:12:42,952 --> 00:12:46,718
<i>Yep, anyone who said our summer</i>
<i>wasn't progressing beautifully</i>

323
00:12:47,077 --> 00:12:49,280
<i>didn't know what</i>
<i>they were talking about.</i>

324
00:12:49,412 --> 00:12:51,460
I'm just saying,
East Indiana State is closer.

325
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:52,574
You gotta consider that.

326
00:12:52,693 --> 00:12:53,795
We still don't know how much
they're gonna play you,

327
00:12:53,901 --> 00:12:55,359
but I like the package
they're putting together.

328
00:12:55,467 --> 00:12:56,543
I don't want to be closer.

329
00:12:56,637 --> 00:12:58,974
I wanna be as far away
from you people as possible.

330
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:02,429
It's like when Tevye decided
his town was too small,

331
00:13:02,537 --> 00:13:04,728
so he went on the flying car
to New York to become a cop.

332
00:13:06,322 --> 00:13:08,172
You do know that's
three separate movies?

333
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:11,049
Dad, I know you're aware

334
00:13:11,181 --> 00:13:13,330
that since the incident
at the drive-in,

335
00:13:13,443 --> 00:13:15,424
I've kinda been
freezing you out.

336
00:13:15,666 --> 00:13:16,884
Mm-hmm?

337
00:13:17,132 --> 00:13:18,831
I guess I just sorta felt
like Serpico

338
00:13:18,948 --> 00:13:20,875
when his toymaker friend
betrayed him,

339
00:13:20,986 --> 00:13:22,922
you know, before the pogrom guys
burned down the wedding.

340
00:13:23,057 --> 00:13:24,582
Again, three separate movies.

341
00:13:24,732 --> 00:13:27,614
My point is, I think I was
blaming you, but I realized

342
00:13:27,730 --> 00:13:30,122
I have to shoulder
the responsibility as well.

343
00:13:30,330 --> 00:13:33,475
Of course it would make sense
that Axl would be your favorite.

344
00:13:33,592 --> 00:13:35,642
You spend more time with him,
and he's a boy and everything,

345
00:13:35,767 --> 00:13:37,121
and I've gotta own that.

346
00:13:37,284 --> 00:13:40,396
Sue, he's not my favorite.
It's just a dumb thing I said.

347
00:13:40,504 --> 00:13:43,667
Owning it. But it's not enough
just to own it.

348
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:46,278
I have to fix it,

349
00:13:46,397 --> 00:13:48,879
and that's why I'm hereby
declaring this

350
00:13:49,709 --> 00:13:52,195
the summer of Sue and dad!

351
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:54,285
Wow!

352
00:13:54,394 --> 00:13:56,147
That's a... big book.

353
00:13:56,242 --> 00:13:59,110
Yes, it is, and you and I are
gonna fill every single page

354
00:13:59,208 --> 00:14:01,731
with special memories
of our summer together.

355
00:14:02,190 --> 00:14:03,508
Memories we make...

356
00:14:03,913 --> 00:14:04,555
starting now.

357
00:14:06,463 --> 00:14:07,932
Aah! <i>Adorbs!</i>

358
00:14:08,033 --> 00:14:09,575
I'm gonna go print it out
right now!

359
00:14:09,878 --> 00:14:10,919
Okay.

360
00:14:14,530 --> 00:14:15,480
Infinite love.

361
00:14:15,596 --> 00:14:16,952
Could've been so easy.

362
00:14:17,994 --> 00:14:19,270
<i>And as the summer wore on,</i>

363
00:14:19,373 --> 00:14:22,346
<i>Mike realized that</i>
<i>more and more.</i>

364
00:14:22,827 --> 00:14:23,926
Pick a color.

365
00:14:24,046 --> 00:14:24,595
Blue.

366
00:14:24,695 --> 00:14:26,668
B-L-U-E. Pick a number.

367
00:14:26,802 --> 00:14:29,134
- Three. - One, two, three.
Pick a higher number.

368
00:14:29,249 --> 00:14:30,730
- Four.
- One, two, three, four.

369
00:14:30,834 --> 00:14:32,207
So then Spencer came back
and was like,

370
00:14:32,305 --> 00:14:34,015
"are you guys going
to the pool?"

371
00:14:34,122 --> 00:14:35,830
and carly thinks
he was asking her out,

372
00:14:35,938 --> 00:14:38,089
but he did say "guys,"
so I'm not sure.

373
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,216
What do you think, dad?

374
00:14:39,329 --> 00:14:41,670
Brad's at tap camp, so I really
need a man's opinion.

375
00:14:41,872 --> 00:14:43,882
Uh...

376
00:14:44,596 --> 00:14:46,459
It's called pass the candle,

377
00:14:46,571 --> 00:14:48,661
and it's a really cool
trust exercise.

378
00:14:48,773 --> 00:14:51,399
We do it at slumber parties
all the time.

379
00:14:51,574 --> 00:14:53,234
I just shared with you

380
00:14:53,522 --> 00:14:55,733
that I don't really like
the feel of sticky tape.

381
00:14:56,052 --> 00:14:59,998
Now it's your turn to share
something with me.

382
00:15:03,927 --> 00:15:05,970
Wait.
Dad, did you make a wish?

383
00:15:06,288 --> 00:15:07,493
Yes.

384
00:15:07,897 --> 00:15:08,955
Yes, I did.

385
00:15:12,987 --> 00:15:15,225
Relax. She's not here.

386
00:15:16,537 --> 00:15:17,513
What are you doing?

387
00:15:17,624 --> 00:15:19,701
Working out and bulking up
at the same time.

388
00:15:19,811 --> 00:15:21,586
I'm the world's
most efficient man.

389
00:15:24,007 --> 00:15:25,093
Axl!

390
00:15:29,109 --> 00:15:31,209
What is this that I just found
under your bed?

391
00:15:31,318 --> 00:15:32,069
I swear it's not mine.

392
00:15:32,173 --> 00:15:34,309
It's a report card
with your name on it.

393
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:35,455
Oh, yeah. That's mine.

394
00:15:36,636 --> 00:15:37,619
Look at this, Mike.

395
00:15:37,715 --> 00:15:41,169
It turns our your favorite son
failed a class.

396
00:15:41,288 --> 00:15:42,964
- What?
- Well, I can explain.

397
00:15:43,111 --> 00:15:44,233
All right,
the first half of the year,

398
00:15:44,338 --> 00:15:45,516
I didn't even know
I was taking it.

399
00:15:45,629 --> 00:15:46,904
I thought I had a free period,

400
00:15:47,025 --> 00:15:49,545
then everyone was too far ahead,
and I was totally lost.

401
00:15:49,697 --> 00:15:50,985
In <i>English?</i>

402
00:15:51,088 --> 00:15:52,579
That shouldn't even be
a requirement.

403
00:15:52,943 --> 00:15:54,370
I've been speaking it,
like, half my life.

404
00:15:54,481 --> 00:15:56,072
How long were you planning
on hiding this from us?

405
00:15:56,207 --> 00:15:57,926
I swear, I was gonna tell you
right after

406
00:15:58,030 --> 00:16:00,762
I did something good,
but nothing good happened, so...

407
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:01,927
If you're gonna sit around
this house

408
00:16:02,028 --> 00:16:03,127
waiting for good things
to happen,

409
00:16:03,232 --> 00:16:05,096
you got a long wait, mister.

410
00:16:05,986 --> 00:16:07,152
What's going on?

411
00:16:07,296 --> 00:16:09,249
Is Axl in some kind of trouble?

412
00:16:09,366 --> 00:16:12,135
Uh, yeah, your brother may not
be going to college.

413
00:16:12,246 --> 00:16:14,998
Chillax. I got, like,
two schools fighting over me.

414
00:16:15,204 --> 00:16:17,600
Not if you don't finish
high school, you don't.

415
00:16:17,728 --> 00:16:20,021
You know, my report card was
quite good.

416
00:16:20,144 --> 00:16:22,018
I could maybe tack it up here
on the fridge

417
00:16:22,136 --> 00:16:23,889
for you to peruse
at your leisure.

418
00:16:24,110 --> 00:16:25,548
It's not that big of a deal.

419
00:16:25,694 --> 00:16:27,737
It's one class.
I can just take it next year.

420
00:16:28,033 --> 00:16:31,454
No, you can't. You've got
a full course load as it is.

421
00:16:31,571 --> 00:16:32,608
Damn it, Axl!

422
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,248
We were gonna spend
one last summer together,

423
00:16:34,369 --> 00:16:35,577
and now I gotta scramble around

424
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:37,831
to see if I can even get you
into summer school!

425
00:16:37,932 --> 00:16:40,369
No! No school in summer.

426
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:42,171
Those things together are
an oxymoron.

427
00:16:42,271 --> 00:16:43,568
Whoa.
I think I used it right.

428
00:16:43,662 --> 00:16:45,031
See? I know this stuff.

429
00:16:45,132 --> 00:16:46,416
The passing grade is
just a formality.

430
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:47,721
Please. Don't make me go
to summer school.

431
00:16:47,855 --> 00:16:49,413
What about
the-- the-- the-- the "this"?

432
00:16:49,534 --> 00:16:51,134
Huh? You said that was
very important.

433
00:16:51,237 --> 00:16:53,033
I'll go outside right now
and hit tennis balls.

434
00:16:53,169 --> 00:16:56,680
Since <i>I</i> got good grades,
I could go do that.

435
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:58,635
Dad, care to join me?

436
00:17:01,515 --> 00:17:04,648
Okay, let me tell you
what's gonna happen now.

437
00:17:04,934 --> 00:17:07,553
You are going to go
to summer school,

438
00:17:07,658 --> 00:17:10,083
and you are going to excel,
or I am gonna reach under

439
00:17:10,183 --> 00:17:13,421
that bed of yours and choke you
with whatever else I find there!

440
00:17:13,499 --> 00:17:15,663
God. That's so typical.

441
00:17:15,797 --> 00:17:16,974
You just focus on
the one bad thing

442
00:17:17,082 --> 00:17:19,262
and completely ignore
all the C's and D's.

443
00:17:28,513 --> 00:17:31,628
Oh, my God. Summer school's
even lamer than real school.

444
00:17:31,881 --> 00:17:34,464
Now they expect me to memorize
a dumb raven poems

445
00:17:34,577 --> 00:17:36,242
that barely even rhyme.
I mean, I could write

446
00:17:36,349 --> 00:17:38,746
a billion times better one
than this right now.

447
00:17:39,682 --> 00:17:42,191
Summer blows. Away it goes.

448
00:17:42,307 --> 00:17:43,489
It's totally sucky...

449
00:17:43,612 --> 00:17:46,274
Something that rhymes
with "sucky."

450
00:17:46,591 --> 00:17:48,422
I think Poe can rest easy
another day.

451
00:17:48,778 --> 00:17:51,300
This is good, guys.
We got here early.

452
00:17:51,407 --> 00:17:53,196
We staked out
a really good spot.

453
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:56,843
Ooh! Yeah, baby!
I love me some fireworks!

454
00:17:56,987 --> 00:17:58,727
Nothing says summer
like fireworks.

455
00:17:58,852 --> 00:18:00,473
Still in there swingin',
huh, pally?

456
00:18:00,603 --> 00:18:01,885
- Mm-hmm.
- Gotta hand it to us.

457
00:18:01,999 --> 00:18:03,562
A lesser family
would've given up.

458
00:18:03,745 --> 00:18:05,685
<i>Is</i> there a lesser family?

459
00:18:06,630 --> 00:18:08,211
Ugh.
There's barely anyone here.

460
00:18:08,403 --> 00:18:10,336
That's because everybody
with lesser parents

461
00:18:10,431 --> 00:18:12,888
are in their houses,
glued to their screens,

462
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:15,861
and we are having
a nice picnic.

463
00:18:15,992 --> 00:18:17,094
Who's got the blue bag?

464
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,293
You forgot the blue bag?

465
00:18:19,396 --> 00:18:21,518
No, I absolutely did not forget
the blue bag.

466
00:18:21,641 --> 00:18:23,166
I pulled it out of the trunk.

467
00:18:27,262 --> 00:18:29,194
Relax. I probably set it
next to the car.

468
00:18:29,284 --> 00:18:30,711
I'll just go back and get it.

469
00:18:31,031 --> 00:18:32,728
Dad, I made up
a bunch of questions

470
00:18:32,824 --> 00:18:33,941
for us to ask each other.

471
00:18:34,061 --> 00:18:36,921
I call it "the summer
of Sue and dad survey,"

472
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:39,967
which when abbreviated
spells "so sad," but it's not.

473
00:18:40,082 --> 00:18:42,150
It's the opposite of that.
It's happy.

474
00:18:42,686 --> 00:18:43,380
Mm.

475
00:18:43,944 --> 00:18:45,149
How long is this gonna last?

476
00:18:45,349 --> 00:18:47,707
Your daughter loving you?
I don't know.

477
00:18:48,543 --> 00:18:50,404
Okay, question one--

478
00:18:50,998 --> 00:18:54,476
Which character on "Glee" do you
most identify with and why?

479
00:18:54,829 --> 00:18:56,805
Dad, wanna go toss
a football around?

480
00:18:56,932 --> 00:18:59,914
Yes.
I think better when I move.

481
00:19:00,044 --> 00:19:00,638
Ooh.

482
00:19:00,729 --> 00:19:02,891
All right, dad, going wide!

483
00:19:03,674 --> 00:19:04,383
Good catch!

484
00:19:04,459 --> 00:19:06,014
You're trying way too hard
with dad, Sue.

485
00:19:06,125 --> 00:19:07,289
It's getting embarrassing.

486
00:19:07,406 --> 00:19:09,365
Uh... I think
the collage I made

487
00:19:09,492 --> 00:19:11,983
of us making collages
would beg to differ.

488
00:19:12,107 --> 00:19:14,552
I have made
a lot of good headway.

489
00:19:14,799 --> 00:19:15,891
Found it.

490
00:19:16,410 --> 00:19:18,976
A few things fell out,
but this chicken is good.

491
00:19:19,124 --> 00:19:19,875
Mmm.

492
00:19:19,971 --> 00:19:21,414
So you're not dad's favorite.

493
00:19:21,598 --> 00:19:23,545
Move on.
I've made peace with it.

494
00:19:23,719 --> 00:19:24,614
Oh, come on.

495
00:19:24,717 --> 00:19:26,225
Are you guys still
talking about this?

496
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:29,906
Look, your dad says stuff,
he doesn't think,

497
00:19:30,011 --> 00:19:32,307
there's no favorites,
he loves you all the same.

498
00:19:32,463 --> 00:19:34,626
How about this kid?
That's my boy!

499
00:19:35,085 --> 00:19:37,724
Axl, get off of dad's shoulders.
It's time to eat.

500
00:19:37,815 --> 00:19:39,369
- All right! Whoo!
- Great pass!

501
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:41,504
Mmm. Triangle watermelon.

502
00:19:41,890 --> 00:19:42,836
My favorite.

503
00:19:43,174 --> 00:19:46,824
See? What'd I tell you? Fruit,
kids, parents, everything.

504
00:19:47,036 --> 00:19:48,200
Parents?

505
00:19:48,485 --> 00:19:50,885
Hells, yeah, parents.
I got favorites.

506
00:19:50,998 --> 00:19:53,892
Like, in terms of you two,
hands down, dad's my favorite.

507
00:19:54,054 --> 00:19:56,102
Axl, we shouldn't do this.

508
00:19:56,221 --> 00:19:58,345
It only ends up
hurting people's feelings.

509
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,165
It's okay, Sue.
I have pretty thick skin.

510
00:20:00,283 --> 00:20:02,228
I mean, of course Axl's gonna
say dad's his favorite.

511
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:03,386
Dad picked him.

512
00:20:03,497 --> 00:20:04,695
They're in cahoots.

513
00:20:04,836 --> 00:20:06,376
I'm not in cahoots with anyone.

514
00:20:06,494 --> 00:20:09,075
This is a silly
discussion to even be having.

515
00:20:09,196 --> 00:20:11,873
Everyone has their own opinions.
Right, guys?

516
00:20:12,831 --> 00:20:14,662
I don't think we should
be talking about this.

517
00:20:14,797 --> 00:20:16,702
No. Go on, Brick.

518
00:20:16,814 --> 00:20:17,918
I think we're all
very interested

519
00:20:18,026 --> 00:20:19,141
in what you have to say.

520
00:20:19,239 --> 00:20:20,831
Look, you have a lot of things
in your favor.

521
00:20:20,948 --> 00:20:22,300
I'm not saying it wasn't
a tough call,

522
00:20:22,415 --> 00:20:23,851
but I gotta go dad.

523
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:25,499
Dad?

524
00:20:25,787 --> 00:20:27,317
This guy right here?

525
00:20:27,436 --> 00:20:29,009
You're the one that nags them.
That's all.

526
00:20:29,104 --> 00:20:30,299
That's the only reason
they're picking me.

527
00:20:30,402 --> 00:20:32,402
This is you defending me?
The nag defense?

528
00:20:32,749 --> 00:20:34,256
You do nag us a lot.

529
00:20:34,356 --> 00:20:35,222
No, you guys.

530
00:20:35,325 --> 00:20:37,579
Stop.
You can't just discount mom.

531
00:20:37,692 --> 00:20:38,941
Mom is there for us.

532
00:20:39,059 --> 00:20:41,032
She does a lot of things for us.

533
00:20:41,159 --> 00:20:42,405
Yeah...

534
00:20:42,539 --> 00:20:44,581
Think about it.
How much does she really do?

535
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,225
I mean, she doesn't cook us
that much food.

536
00:20:46,334 --> 00:20:47,984
Then again,
do we really want her to?

537
00:20:48,086 --> 00:20:49,545
This chicken's pretty rank.

538
00:20:49,905 --> 00:20:51,047
I like it.

539
00:20:51,135 --> 00:20:52,131
That is true.

540
00:20:52,231 --> 00:20:54,087
Your after-school
pickup record's a little spotty.

541
00:20:54,192 --> 00:20:55,405
She's not the most reliable.

542
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:56,917
She did leave me
at wrestlerette practice

543
00:20:57,012 --> 00:20:59,217
so late the janitor went home
and my hair froze.

544
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,731
It was one time.
I fell asleep.

545
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:02,789
Come on. You were going

546
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:04,590
in the right direction
there before, Sue.

547
00:21:04,694 --> 00:21:06,528
Just stand up for yourself
and your beliefs.

548
00:21:06,634 --> 00:21:08,673
Yeah, just say it, Sue.
Who's your favorite?

549
00:21:08,787 --> 00:21:10,687
I am not gonna do this.
I am not gonna participate

550
00:21:10,791 --> 00:21:13,118
in anything that's just gonna
end up hurting mom's feelings.

551
00:21:15,455 --> 00:21:16,590
I'm sorry, mom.

552
00:21:16,707 --> 00:21:18,230
I am so, so sorry.

553
00:21:18,385 --> 00:21:21,760
It's just that it's
the summer of Sue and <i>dad.</i>

554
00:21:22,174 --> 00:21:23,356
Wow.

555
00:21:23,974 --> 00:21:26,075
Wow. Wow. Wow. Wow. Wow.

556
00:21:26,316 --> 00:21:27,974
So you're not
their favorite parent.

557
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,021
You're a solid second place.

558
00:21:30,866 --> 00:21:33,023
- Eh.
- Eh?

559
00:21:33,136 --> 00:21:35,497
Mrs. Donahue sends Sean with
extra cookies for my lunch.

560
00:21:35,613 --> 00:21:36,676
Hang on. This is wrong.

561
00:21:36,802 --> 00:21:38,571
None of us are being fair
to mom here.

562
00:21:38,728 --> 00:21:40,581
Maybe if you made your case.

563
00:21:40,919 --> 00:21:44,108
Oh, please.
I am not gonna make my case.

564
00:21:45,072 --> 00:21:46,212
Okay, fine.

565
00:21:46,404 --> 00:21:49,540
First of all, I'm the one that
does all things kid-related.

566
00:21:49,673 --> 00:21:51,034
I sign
all your permission slips,

567
00:21:51,151 --> 00:21:52,679
I run out
and get you poster board,

568
00:21:52,802 --> 00:21:55,492
I clean that cesspool
you call a backpack.

569
00:21:55,623 --> 00:21:56,291
Frankie, don't do this.

570
00:21:56,384 --> 00:21:58,117
Oh, I'm doing it.
Do you know

571
00:21:58,218 --> 00:22:01,088
all three of your heads
were unnaturally large,

572
00:22:01,215 --> 00:22:03,228
thanks to your giant
favorite parent over here's

573
00:22:03,326 --> 00:22:04,655
weird genetic quirk?

574
00:22:04,762 --> 00:22:07,675
And that after 27 months
of carrying you people around,

575
00:22:07,788 --> 00:22:10,404
I can no longer sneeze or laugh
or jump in the bouncy house

576
00:22:10,526 --> 00:22:11,992
without peeing?

577
00:22:12,192 --> 00:22:13,512
They don't really
need to know that.

578
00:22:13,610 --> 00:22:15,024
Okay. What about tonight?

579
00:22:15,165 --> 00:22:16,542
Who's the one
that got us out of the house,

580
00:22:16,695 --> 00:22:19,157
that packed the blue bag
full of tasty chicken,

581
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:21,416
and searched the newspapers
for the best park

582
00:22:21,543 --> 00:22:23,420
with the best view
of the best fireworks,

583
00:22:23,519 --> 00:22:27,056
all so we could create one
stinking memory of <i>"this"?</i>

584
00:22:27,161 --> 00:22:29,810
Well, if anybody's
still confused, it was me.

585
00:22:30,055 --> 00:22:31,405
Me, me, me.

586
00:22:31,508 --> 00:22:34,418
So just lie down, stop talking,
and start watching,

587
00:22:34,531 --> 00:22:38,102
because nothing says summer
like fireworks!

588
00:22:48,843 --> 00:22:51,991
Nobody... say...
anything.

589
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:02,848
<i>As July turned into August,</i>

590
00:23:02,973 --> 00:23:04,230
<i>the only healthy relationship</i>

591
00:23:04,323 --> 00:23:07,064
<i>left in the house</i>
<i>was Brick and his tomato.</i>

592
00:23:07,890 --> 00:23:10,839
<i>It grew so big he needed</i>
<i>to find support for it.</i>

593
00:23:11,866 --> 00:23:12,901
Brick!

594
00:23:13,017 --> 00:23:15,180
<i>And then he found other support</i>
<i>for it.</i>

595
00:23:16,078 --> 00:23:17,204
Brick!

596
00:23:18,834 --> 00:23:20,884
<i>I'd like to say we were</i>
<i>making the same progress</i>

597
00:23:20,985 --> 00:23:22,383
<i>on our summer...</i>

598
00:23:22,469 --> 00:23:24,552
<i>But I wasn't throwing in</i>
<i>the towel just yet.</i>

599
00:23:24,677 --> 00:23:27,745
Guys, come on.
It's a beautiful day out there,

600
00:23:27,868 --> 00:23:30,656
and I'm about to show you
some real fun.

601
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:32,230
Guess what I used to do
when I was a kid.

602
00:23:32,361 --> 00:23:33,921
Ride dinosaurs?

603
00:23:34,125 --> 00:23:36,198
Yes, 'cause I'm
a billion years old.

604
00:23:36,328 --> 00:23:38,048
Come on. You're gonna love it.

605
00:23:42,586 --> 00:23:43,854
Ta-da!

606
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,122
What are we supposed to do?

607
00:23:46,302 --> 00:23:47,614
Run through it.

608
00:23:48,264 --> 00:23:49,241
Why?

609
00:23:49,362 --> 00:23:50,551
Because it's fun.

610
00:23:50,682 --> 00:23:52,010
Come on. I'll show you.

611
00:23:52,710 --> 00:23:53,969
Whoo-hoo! Whoo!

612
00:23:55,094 --> 00:23:56,472
What do you do now?

613
00:23:56,627 --> 00:23:58,146
You run through it again,
like...

614
00:23:58,266 --> 00:24:02,521
Whoa! Whoa! It's cold,
but exhilarating.

615
00:24:02,761 --> 00:24:04,012
I don't get it.

616
00:24:04,137 --> 00:24:04,947
- Please stop.
- Me neither.

617
00:24:05,056 --> 00:24:06,916
No, try it.
Listen if your clothes get wet,

618
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:09,454
I won't freak out on you
like your dad would.

619
00:24:09,611 --> 00:24:11,810
Come on.
It's-- it's spontaneous.

620
00:24:11,911 --> 00:24:13,245
Just... Whoo!

621
00:24:13,339 --> 00:24:14,725
You can go slow

622
00:24:15,022 --> 00:24:17,165
or you can go fast. Aah!

623
00:24:17,877 --> 00:24:19,329
Skip...

624
00:24:21,366 --> 00:24:22,857
You can go backwards.

625
00:24:23,635 --> 00:24:24,885
Whoo! Ooh.

626
00:24:24,977 --> 00:24:26,804
You can pretend like you're
leaping into another dimension.

627
00:24:32,464 --> 00:24:33,328
Oh, sure.

628
00:24:33,423 --> 00:24:35,910
If your dad suggested it,
you would do it.

629
00:24:36,179 --> 00:24:38,848
Well, I'm not playing
this popularity contest.

630
00:24:38,944 --> 00:24:40,565
Yeah, I'm not.

631
00:24:40,719 --> 00:24:41,482
You know, Brick,

632
00:24:41,572 --> 00:24:43,732
I always thought you and I
had a special bond. Hmm?

633
00:24:43,925 --> 00:24:46,922
Mother and son--
no stronger bond on earth.

634
00:24:47,031 --> 00:24:49,487
Really? I thought you believed
in infinite love.

635
00:24:49,908 --> 00:24:51,676
Well, yes,

636
00:24:51,886 --> 00:24:54,298
infinite love
while also understanding

637
00:24:54,456 --> 00:24:57,895
that you might have a special
connection to one person

638
00:24:58,069 --> 00:25:01,705
or parent more than the other.

639
00:25:01,868 --> 00:25:04,046
And here's the thing.
I know you probably felt

640
00:25:04,151 --> 00:25:05,964
the pressure to say dad was
your favorite

641
00:25:06,083 --> 00:25:08,738
'cause that's the way the whole
family seemed to be leaning,

642
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:10,410
but honestly,

643
00:25:10,543 --> 00:25:13,069
I think it takes real character

644
00:25:13,188 --> 00:25:16,238
to speak out and express
your own feelings,

645
00:25:16,375 --> 00:25:19,442
and I think that you have
that kind of character.

646
00:25:20,650 --> 00:25:21,945
Mom, you're better than this.

647
00:25:22,047 --> 00:25:23,967
I'm not, though, Brick.
I'm really not.

648
00:25:24,059 --> 00:25:26,480
This is killing me. How could
you pick dad over me?

649
00:25:26,590 --> 00:25:28,100
He says it's okay if my socks
don't match.

650
00:25:28,196 --> 00:25:29,958
But it's not! Because people
will think you're weird,

651
00:25:30,094 --> 00:25:33,371
and I'm only telling you that
'cause I love you more than dad.

652
00:25:33,591 --> 00:25:34,807
It's 'cause he's tall.

653
00:25:34,912 --> 00:25:36,815
People love tall people.
I've seen the studies.

654
00:25:36,924 --> 00:25:38,239
Look, to be honest,

655
00:25:38,336 --> 00:25:40,673
I think the fireworks thing
really set you back.

656
00:25:40,824 --> 00:25:43,771
I mean, you literally robbed us
of fire in the sky.

657
00:25:43,962 --> 00:25:45,835
Plus, we all got sick
from your chicken.

658
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:48,808
That was a month ago. What,
are you guys keeping score?

659
00:25:48,939 --> 00:25:51,292
32 to 10. And if it was up
to Axl and Sue,

660
00:25:51,409 --> 00:25:52,749
you'd only have 4 points.

661
00:25:56,913 --> 00:25:58,626
- Brick, does dad know you're--
- Oh, don't worry.

662
00:25:58,756 --> 00:26:01,018
They're not dad's. I found them
on the playground.

663
00:26:04,612 --> 00:26:05,655
All right.

664
00:26:07,626 --> 00:26:10,563
So, uh, listen,
just off the top of my head,

665
00:26:10,734 --> 00:26:12,870
you know, totally unrelated
to this discussion,

666
00:26:13,186 --> 00:26:14,676
summer's almost over.

667
00:26:14,896 --> 00:26:16,045
So if there's anything,

668
00:26:16,185 --> 00:26:19,140
anything at all
that you wanted to do,

669
00:26:20,126 --> 00:26:22,820
I'd certainly do my best
to try and make it happen.

670
00:26:23,210 --> 00:26:24,316
Really?

671
00:26:24,437 --> 00:26:25,740
Well, actually,

672
00:26:25,931 --> 00:26:28,178
I read that
the River County fair is

673
00:26:28,285 --> 00:26:29,934
having a big tomato contest.

674
00:26:30,138 --> 00:26:31,513
The winner gets a trophy

675
00:26:31,634 --> 00:26:33,724
and a shout-out
on the River Soil web site.

676
00:26:33,868 --> 00:26:37,189
Ugh. Brick,
it's three hours away.

677
00:26:37,577 --> 00:26:39,393
It'll probably get you
20 points.

678
00:26:39,966 --> 00:26:41,718
Fine.

679
00:26:43,194 --> 00:26:44,582
Dad, so glad you're home.

680
00:26:44,718 --> 00:26:46,499
I got markers, stencils,
and jewels,

681
00:26:46,602 --> 00:26:48,174
and I thought we could
each make a page

682
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:50,104
for the "summer of Sue and dad"
book,

683
00:26:50,204 --> 00:26:51,878
but we don't know
what the other is doing,

684
00:26:51,971 --> 00:26:53,647
and then we dedicate 'em
to each other.

685
00:26:53,754 --> 00:26:56,582
Hang on, Sue.
Axl, what are you doing?

686
00:26:56,899 --> 00:26:58,835
I am pen face.

687
00:27:00,137 --> 00:27:01,847
Well, be book face
and start studying.

688
00:27:01,945 --> 00:27:03,591
You got a lot of material
to cover by Friday.

689
00:27:03,684 --> 00:27:06,326
Uh, how many times have <i>you</i>
taken eleventh grade English?

690
00:27:06,411 --> 00:27:07,455
'Cause I've taken it twice now,

691
00:27:07,593 --> 00:27:09,800
so I think I know
a little bit more than you.

692
00:27:09,923 --> 00:27:11,476
Dad, glitter glue
or sharpie markers?

693
00:27:11,626 --> 00:27:13,140
Oh, is that so? Okay.

694
00:27:13,244 --> 00:27:14,380
Let's take a little quiz.

695
00:27:14,754 --> 00:27:16,539
In the first act
of "Death of a Salesman,"

696
00:27:16,699 --> 00:27:18,000
which character--

697
00:27:18,104 --> 00:27:19,528
Death.

698
00:27:19,901 --> 00:27:23,146
Death isn't even
a character, Axl.

699
00:27:24,364 --> 00:27:25,324
That's fine.

700
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:27,527
I guess we'll just sit here
and go over this together.

701
00:27:27,939 --> 00:27:30,302
<i>And it was at that moment,</i>
<i>Sue realized...</i>

702
00:27:30,421 --> 00:27:32,933
<i>Attention didn't have to be</i>
<i>positive,</i>

703
00:27:33,674 --> 00:27:34,949
<i>and maybe negative attention</i>

704
00:27:35,094 --> 00:27:37,435
<i>was better than no attention</i>
<i>at all.</i>

705
00:27:37,971 --> 00:27:41,169
<i>So Sue set out to explore</i>
<i>her dark side.</i>

706
00:27:41,605 --> 00:27:43,510
<i>Well, dark for Sue.</i>

707
00:27:43,927 --> 00:27:45,456
<i>She used Mike's razor...</i>

708
00:27:45,602 --> 00:27:46,662
Ah!

709
00:27:47,861 --> 00:27:49,603
Not using a coaster.

710
00:27:49,752 --> 00:27:52,149
Nope. Hot day, too.

711
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:53,636
Whatevs.

712
00:27:56,825 --> 00:27:58,712
<i>She didn't wind up the hose...</i>

713
00:28:04,198 --> 00:28:05,766
<i>And worst of all...</i>

714
00:28:05,889 --> 00:28:07,909
Going to bed
without my headgear,

715
00:28:08,059 --> 00:28:09,227
even though the orthodontist

716
00:28:09,319 --> 00:28:11,257
totally recommends
I wear it at night.

717
00:28:12,751 --> 00:28:15,180
But I don't care. Whatevs.

718
00:28:17,407 --> 00:28:19,778
<i>So as we headed into</i>
<i>the final few days of summer,</i>

719
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,164
<i>we were all frustrated,</i>

720
00:28:22,279 --> 00:28:24,932
<i>but we had one more chance</i>
<i>to salvage the summer--</i>

721
00:28:25,024 --> 00:28:26,556
<i>the River County fair.</i>

722
00:28:27,218 --> 00:28:29,892
Hey, gentle
on the bumps, please.

723
00:28:30,009 --> 00:28:32,711
I can't believe this. I finally
finish my last English paper

724
00:28:32,837 --> 00:28:34,844
while we're pumping gas,
and instead of taking me out

725
00:28:34,953 --> 00:28:36,093
or buying me a reward,

726
00:28:36,192 --> 00:28:39,462
I'm stuck chauffeuring a tomato
to a loser fest.

727
00:28:39,584 --> 00:28:40,682
This is a big deal.

728
00:28:40,794 --> 00:28:42,893
There was a whole write-up
about last year's.

729
00:28:43,009 --> 00:28:44,251
Listen to this--

730
00:28:44,922 --> 00:28:48,271
"As gawkers lined past
the table full of tomatoes,

731
00:28:48,423 --> 00:28:49,879
they were heard to exclaim,

732
00:28:50,010 --> 00:28:52,772
'well, I never saw anything
like this,'

733
00:28:52,935 --> 00:28:56,131
and 'I think this one's
gonna be a winner.'"

734
00:28:56,244 --> 00:28:57,269
Aah!

735
00:28:57,378 --> 00:28:58,816
Axl, come on.

736
00:28:58,966 --> 00:29:01,078
This could be our last summer
together as a family.

737
00:29:01,227 --> 00:29:02,750
Don't you want
to get some of "this"

738
00:29:02,872 --> 00:29:04,882
before you're out there
dealing with all that?

739
00:29:04,982 --> 00:29:06,610
Oh, my God.
Isn't "this" over yet?

740
00:29:06,762 --> 00:29:08,526
It's not this. It's "this."

741
00:29:08,617 --> 00:29:10,986
Well, I want to do this,
this, and...

742
00:29:11,126 --> 00:29:12,690
This.

743
00:29:13,718 --> 00:29:16,555
You know, dad, I'm not surprised
you wanted to drive together

744
00:29:16,658 --> 00:29:18,676
so you could talk to me alone.

745
00:29:20,274 --> 00:29:22,652
What are you talking about?
I had to stop at work first,

746
00:29:22,769 --> 00:29:24,448
and you said
you wanted to come with me.

747
00:29:24,824 --> 00:29:27,720
I get it.
I've been out of control.

748
00:29:28,364 --> 00:29:31,151
I'm sure you're very
disappointed in my behavior.

749
00:29:31,959 --> 00:29:34,890
Well, you've been sort of
annoying with that scrapbook.

750
00:29:35,012 --> 00:29:36,471
No, it's good
you're intervening now,

751
00:29:36,578 --> 00:29:38,124
'cause I am at a crucial point
in my life

752
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:39,924
where I could go either way.

753
00:29:46,081 --> 00:29:47,034
♪ Do-do-do-do ♪

754
00:29:47,136 --> 00:29:49,253
♪ do-do-do-do ♪

755
00:29:53,268 --> 00:29:54,051
I mean,

756
00:29:54,185 --> 00:29:55,375
I stopped taking
my multivitamins,

757
00:29:55,479 --> 00:29:57,326
so I don't know
where that's gonna lead.

758
00:29:57,489 --> 00:30:00,179
Yep. Probably got a lot
of attention headed my way,

759
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,449
and not the good kind.

760
00:30:06,614 --> 00:30:08,254
I've done some bad things, dad.

761
00:30:08,372 --> 00:30:09,452
Bad things.

762
00:30:09,550 --> 00:30:10,815
Yesterday I was
at a health fair,

763
00:30:10,921 --> 00:30:12,258
and there was a booth
with a basket of chapstick,

764
00:30:12,375 --> 00:30:13,276
and I took one.

765
00:30:13,380 --> 00:30:15,075
Maybe they weren't even free.

766
00:30:15,224 --> 00:30:16,515
I don't know.

767
00:30:16,629 --> 00:30:18,984
They could've been for sale,
and I just shoplifted.

768
00:30:19,113 --> 00:30:20,248
Whatevs.

769
00:30:21,016 --> 00:30:22,223
Oh, God. Oh!

770
00:30:25,883 --> 00:30:28,316
I think I'm gonna throw up.

771
00:30:28,496 --> 00:30:30,964
You didn't eat the ham sandwich
that was in that towel, did you?

772
00:30:31,182 --> 00:30:32,573
I'm just nervous.

773
00:30:32,697 --> 00:30:34,967
I heard there's out-of-towners
from Des Moines coming in,

774
00:30:35,092 --> 00:30:37,028
and they had above-average
rainfall this year.

775
00:30:37,225 --> 00:30:39,302
Axl, let us out.
I gotta give Brick some air.

776
00:30:39,403 --> 00:30:41,149
Just park the car and meet us
at the funnel cake stand.

777
00:30:41,257 --> 00:30:42,871
Don't say "funnel cake."

778
00:30:43,297 --> 00:30:44,739
Funnel cake.

779
00:30:45,709 --> 00:30:46,502
Oh.

780
00:30:47,783 --> 00:30:49,151
You here
for the demolition derby?

781
00:30:49,472 --> 00:30:51,029
Uh, yeah. Sure.

782
00:30:51,139 --> 00:30:53,094
Okay. This way.

783
00:31:05,876 --> 00:31:09,181
What the...
Hey! Get back here!

784
00:31:11,793 --> 00:31:12,917
Are you kidding me?

785
00:31:13,923 --> 00:31:15,741
This is
the worst parking lot ever.

786
00:31:16,090 --> 00:31:17,936
I'm gonna need
your insurance card!

787
00:31:23,114 --> 00:31:24,825
<i>Who's gonna win this time?</i>

788
00:31:29,629 --> 00:31:31,363
<i>Number 11...</i>

789
00:31:40,921 --> 00:31:44,185
This worked out just the way
you wanted, didn't it, Axl?

790
00:31:44,336 --> 00:31:45,802
You saw that he was a champion,

791
00:31:45,929 --> 00:31:47,696
and you couldn't take
that somebody else

792
00:31:47,813 --> 00:31:49,440
was gonna get the glory.

793
00:31:49,688 --> 00:31:52,361
You are
a small, small, petty man.

794
00:31:52,468 --> 00:31:54,345
God, Brick, it was an accident!
What about my car?

795
00:31:54,455 --> 00:31:56,700
Who drives a car into
a demolition derby by mistake?

796
00:31:56,792 --> 00:31:57,957
At least I placed fourth.

797
00:31:58,062 --> 00:31:59,840
If it wasn't for sergeant
smashup, I would've medaled.

798
00:31:59,943 --> 00:32:01,401
Listen, everybody,
just take a breath.

799
00:32:01,506 --> 00:32:02,544
This is nothing
we can't work out

800
00:32:02,660 --> 00:32:04,326
over a couple
of fried snickers, okay?

801
00:32:04,431 --> 00:32:06,260
Last Sunday, in church,
when the priest told us

802
00:32:06,368 --> 00:32:08,652
to pray for the poor, you know,
I-I prayed for the rich.

803
00:32:08,785 --> 00:32:10,961
That's just the way my brain is
working these days.

804
00:32:11,153 --> 00:32:15,171
I cannot believe that you would
do something so moronic.

805
00:32:15,282 --> 00:32:16,527
As I said,
we could all use a minute.

806
00:32:16,621 --> 00:32:18,915
Let's just get a fried pie,
a couple fried marshmallows.

807
00:32:19,021 --> 00:32:21,070
There's a fried butter stand
right in there. Come on.

808
00:32:21,178 --> 00:32:22,529
Oh. The car.

809
00:32:22,986 --> 00:32:24,461
Axl, I said we're not
talking about--

810
00:32:24,557 --> 00:32:27,105
No, my paper's in that car!
My final paper I need to turn in

811
00:32:27,218 --> 00:32:29,123
to pass
my stupid summer school class!

812
00:32:29,700 --> 00:32:31,303
- Damn it, Axl!
- Axl, are you kidding?!

813
00:32:31,455 --> 00:32:33,245
I ate unwashed fruit!

814
00:32:33,364 --> 00:32:34,090
Wait!

815
00:32:34,182 --> 00:32:35,386
Well, I'm not helping.

816
00:32:35,495 --> 00:32:36,543
Hey! Wait!

817
00:32:36,619 --> 00:32:37,956
No, I'm not gonna help
go get it,

818
00:32:38,049 --> 00:32:39,134
even if somebody asks me...

819
00:32:39,983 --> 00:32:41,368
- Stop! Come back!
- Wait!

820
00:32:41,495 --> 00:32:42,534
...to.

821
00:32:43,996 --> 00:32:45,877
<i>As Sue watched the family</i>
<i>take off,</i>

822
00:32:46,075 --> 00:32:48,607
<i>she realized that whether</i>
<i>she joined us or not,</i>

823
00:32:49,094 --> 00:32:50,518
<i>no one would notice.</i>

824
00:32:51,062 --> 00:32:53,855
<i>The only way she was gonna</i>
<i>get our attention was to...</i>

825
00:32:54,242 --> 00:32:55,707
<i>disappear.</i>

826
00:33:08,859 --> 00:33:11,616
<i>So Sue walked the midway</i>
<i>for what seemed like forever,</i>

827
00:33:12,821 --> 00:33:14,405
<i>trying to get lost,</i>

828
00:33:15,102 --> 00:33:16,867
<i>but hoping to be found.</i>

829
00:33:24,988 --> 00:33:26,120
Hi.

830
00:33:26,249 --> 00:33:27,649
Uh, my name is Sue Heck.

831
00:33:27,788 --> 00:33:29,795
Has anyone tried
to find me yet?

832
00:33:30,247 --> 00:33:32,602
No. I don't think so.

833
00:33:32,945 --> 00:33:34,115
Are you lost?

834
00:33:34,233 --> 00:33:35,712
Well, no, not yet.

835
00:33:36,050 --> 00:33:37,649
But probably soon.

836
00:33:39,675 --> 00:33:41,440
I'll just wait over here.

837
00:33:53,209 --> 00:33:56,100
So if someone was
trying to find me,

838
00:33:56,427 --> 00:33:58,960
<i>this</i> is where'd they come.
Correct?

839
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:00,962
Yes.

840
00:34:01,096 --> 00:34:02,625
Okay.

841
00:34:10,046 --> 00:34:11,923
Are you here
'cause you're in trouble?

842
00:34:12,070 --> 00:34:13,243
Oh. No. No, no, no, no.

843
00:34:13,363 --> 00:34:14,756
I-I'm a nice girl.

844
00:34:14,913 --> 00:34:16,977
Oh. See?

845
00:34:23,953 --> 00:34:26,785
You know,
it's a really crowded fair,

846
00:34:26,894 --> 00:34:28,417
so sometimes it takes them
a while

847
00:34:28,521 --> 00:34:30,100
to notice you're missing.

848
00:34:31,659 --> 00:34:33,211
Oscar, thank God!

849
00:34:33,395 --> 00:34:35,817
Oh. That was the longest
four minutes of our lives.

850
00:34:35,917 --> 00:34:37,750
We don't know what we would've
done without you.

851
00:34:37,853 --> 00:34:39,712
Never do that to us again.

852
00:34:40,335 --> 00:34:42,668
All right. Let's get
some ice cream.

853
00:34:53,143 --> 00:34:55,131
It's ringing.

854
00:34:56,595 --> 00:34:59,379
If you guys are home,
um, this is Sue,

855
00:34:59,538 --> 00:35:03,110
and I'm still at the fair,
so...

856
00:35:03,238 --> 00:35:05,273
Hi. We lost something
very important.

857
00:35:05,438 --> 00:35:07,015
Our son's English paper.

858
00:35:07,130 --> 00:35:08,934
It was in one of the cars
they hauled away to the dump.

859
00:35:09,045 --> 00:35:10,590
We tried to chase it down,
but we couldn't catch it,

860
00:35:10,705 --> 00:35:12,322
and then we went
to the demolition derby arena,

861
00:35:12,437 --> 00:35:13,533
but they told us to come here.

862
00:35:13,647 --> 00:35:16,663
I need that paper. I can't take
junior English a third time.

863
00:35:16,792 --> 00:35:18,077
I just can't.

864
00:35:18,216 --> 00:35:20,762
I'm just an hourly hire.
Sorry.

865
00:35:24,403 --> 00:35:26,626
Sue, we're all tired
from running around,

866
00:35:26,743 --> 00:35:28,799
but this is no time to sit.
Let's go.

867
00:35:35,651 --> 00:35:38,089
<i>With Axl's car demolished,</i>
<i>his paper gone,</i>

868
00:35:38,226 --> 00:35:41,280
<i>Brick's tomato squashed,</i>
<i>and Sue in a dark place,</i>

869
00:35:41,422 --> 00:35:43,828
<i>the end of summer was a bust.</i>

870
00:35:44,191 --> 00:35:45,770
<i>There weren't enough foods</i>
<i>on a stick</i>

871
00:35:45,882 --> 00:35:47,513
<i>to turn this thing around.</i>

872
00:35:48,038 --> 00:35:50,250
- Anybody wanna check out the fun house?
- No.

873
00:35:50,487 --> 00:35:51,823
4-H beef show?

874
00:35:51,950 --> 00:35:52,875
No.

875
00:35:52,983 --> 00:35:54,971
The cheesy side dish
judging contest?

876
00:35:55,086 --> 00:35:56,245
No.

877
00:35:56,524 --> 00:35:59,815
Frankie, can we just pull
the rip cord on this thing?

878
00:35:59,952 --> 00:36:02,124
Let's just admit that
our amazing summer was a bust

879
00:36:02,251 --> 00:36:05,264
and hope fall is
a little kinder to us.

880
00:36:05,379 --> 00:36:07,807
- I was at lost and found, and no one
knew I was gone. - I just wanna go home.

881
00:36:07,912 --> 00:36:10,743
Fine. I was just trying
'cause that's what you wanted.

882
00:36:10,856 --> 00:36:13,238
If you're done, I'm done.
Let's just go to the car.

883
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:38,254
- Really?
- I don't believe this.

884
00:36:38,379 --> 00:36:40,039
I always remember where I park.

885
00:36:40,154 --> 00:36:42,401
I hope you guys are
deducting points for this.

886
00:36:42,522 --> 00:36:44,967
I think it was near a white van.
Sue, do you remember?

887
00:36:45,178 --> 00:36:47,282
Oh, I'm sorry.
Were you talking to me?

888
00:36:47,397 --> 00:36:49,985
I'm tired and emotionally
drained. Where's the car?

889
00:36:50,095 --> 00:36:53,509
I don't know. Sue was talking
a lot when we parked.

890
00:36:53,710 --> 00:36:54,961
Nice going, dad.

891
00:36:55,428 --> 00:36:56,882
Oh, yeah? Really?

892
00:36:56,988 --> 00:36:59,219
Well, at least I got a car
to drive home in.

893
00:36:59,333 --> 00:37:01,489
Oh, ho, like you've never
accidentally driven your car

894
00:37:01,591 --> 00:37:03,474
into a demolition derby before.

895
00:37:03,577 --> 00:37:05,350
No. You know what, Axl?
I haven't.

896
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:07,215
God, you've been so grumpy
all day.

897
00:37:07,330 --> 00:37:10,102
- Gee. I wonder if there's a reason why.
- I don't know what you want me to say.

898
00:37:10,227 --> 00:37:11,600
I'll save up for a new car.

899
00:37:11,700 --> 00:37:14,431
This isn't about the car,
Axl. This is about you.

900
00:37:14,592 --> 00:37:16,400
<i>Of course</i> it is.

901
00:37:16,511 --> 00:37:18,259
Do you realize that if you
would've gotten hurt,

902
00:37:18,376 --> 00:37:20,725
you could've kissed your
football scholarship good-bye?

903
00:37:20,914 --> 00:37:22,788
You gotta start being smart.

904
00:37:22,923 --> 00:37:24,391
I try, but it's not that easy.

905
00:37:24,515 --> 00:37:26,203
Well, I'm tired of being smart
<i>for</i> you.

906
00:37:26,310 --> 00:37:28,469
This is your entire future here,
and you're playing games

907
00:37:28,586 --> 00:37:30,632
with your report card
and almost getting killed.

908
00:37:30,748 --> 00:37:33,572
You're 18. It's time for you
to start doing the thinking.

909
00:37:33,725 --> 00:37:36,085
I always think
I'm very responsible.

910
00:37:36,208 --> 00:37:38,429
You don't know how lucky you are
to have a scholarship.

911
00:37:38,829 --> 00:37:41,050
I'd have killed to play ball
in college.

912
00:37:41,167 --> 00:37:44,301
He doesn't care. He has no
respect for people or produce.

913
00:37:44,410 --> 00:37:46,526
Oh, that was not my fault.
All right, you blame mom

914
00:37:46,629 --> 00:37:48,107
for dragging us here
in the first place.

915
00:37:48,221 --> 00:37:49,927
Hey, me, your nonfavorite,

916
00:37:50,024 --> 00:37:52,404
was fine with you watching TV
all summer.

917
00:37:52,505 --> 00:37:54,490
He's the one
that wanted you off it.

918
00:37:54,601 --> 00:37:56,143
I would've preferred TV
to coming here.

919
00:37:56,269 --> 00:37:58,472
Oh, you're the one
that wanted "this."

920
00:37:58,577 --> 00:38:00,145
I was just trying
to give it to you.

921
00:38:00,264 --> 00:38:03,379
Oh, no. No, this has nothing
to do with "this."

922
00:38:03,497 --> 00:38:04,951
The only reason we're here is

923
00:38:05,076 --> 00:38:06,809
'cause you wanted
to suck up to Brick.

924
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:09,279
That's right. I know
all about the 20 points.

925
00:38:09,448 --> 00:38:11,327
Well, I'm done with summer.

926
00:38:11,475 --> 00:38:14,776
But this was supposed to be
the summer of Sue and dad!

927
00:38:14,881 --> 00:38:16,882
Sue! Enough already.

928
00:38:16,982 --> 00:38:19,064
I love you, damn it.
I shouldn't have to say it.

929
00:38:30,931 --> 00:38:35,101
<i>So it turnout it's impossible</i>
<i>to stay mad during fireworks.</i>

930
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:36,421
<i>You just can't.</i>

931
00:38:36,540 --> 00:38:38,776
<i>It's literally fire in the sky.</i>

932
00:38:38,876 --> 00:38:40,394
- Oh!
- Oh!

933
00:38:41,207 --> 00:38:42,631
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

934
00:38:43,461 --> 00:38:46,573
- Oh, that's pretty.
- The pinwheel ones-- I love those.

935
00:38:46,686 --> 00:38:47,564
Me, too.

936
00:38:47,697 --> 00:38:49,011
- Oh!
- Oh!

937
00:38:50,740 --> 00:38:53,521
<i>The thing is, you can't force</i>
<i>a great summer.</i>

938
00:38:54,732 --> 00:38:56,706
<i>It just happens.</i>

939
00:38:59,906 --> 00:39:01,540
Wait. I think I got it.

940
00:39:03,374 --> 00:39:04,926
Make sure your thumbs
are right.

941
00:39:05,040 --> 00:39:06,383
It's all in the thumbs.

942
00:39:07,834 --> 00:39:09,133
- Hey.
- Epic.

943
00:39:18,460 --> 00:39:20,534
<i>I gotta say,</i>
<i>of all our summers,</i>

944
00:39:20,709 --> 00:39:23,410
<i>that one might've ended up</i>
<i>being my favorite.</i>

945
00:39:23,555 --> 00:39:25,486
<i>Not that I have any favorites.</i>

946
00:39:33,302 --> 00:39:36,234
♪ Trees ♪

947
00:39:36,333 --> 00:39:39,571
♪ swayin' in the summer breeze ♪

948
00:39:39,810 --> 00:39:43,168
♪ showin' off
their silver leaves ♪

949
00:39:43,301 --> 00:39:45,874
♪ as we walked by ♪

950
00:39:45,969 --> 00:39:47,732
♪ soft ♪

951
00:39:47,830 --> 00:39:50,700
♪ kisses on a summer's day ♪

952
00:39:51,217 --> 00:39:54,546
♪ laughin' all our cares away ♪

953
00:39:54,866 --> 00:39:57,482
♪ just you and I ♪

954
00:40:28,647 --> 00:40:34,000
